                        {product.cons.map((con) => (
                          <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-red-800">
                            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-red-500 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"></path></svg>
                            {con}
                          </li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100">
                    <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500 mb-1">The Bottom Line</p>
                    <p class="text-gray-900 font-bold">{product.bottomLine}</p>
                  </div>

                  <a
                    href={amazonLink(product.amazonUrl, product.name, product.id)}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"
                    class="mt-6 block bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white text-center py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm"
                  >
                    Check Price &rarr;
                  </a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div id="hands-on" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Christmas Gift Ideas for Men Who Work With Their Hands
          </h2>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">For the DIYer and the garage guy</h3>

          <p>
            The best tool gifts solve a problem he already has. If he does not own a cordless drill, the <a href="/best-cordless-drill-for-home-use/">Craftsman V20 combo kit</a> is the answer, because it arrives with two tools, two batteries and a charger and needs nothing else. If he already owns a drill, do not buy him another one; find out which battery platform he uses and buy a bare tool on it, or choose something he would never think to buy, like a proper stud finder or a torque wrench.
          </p>

          <p>
            That is why the <a href="/best-stud-finder/">Franklin ProSensor M210</a> is on this list. It is a modest gift with an outsized effect, because it ends the habit of knocking on walls and guessing. For the man who works on cars, the GearWrench electronic wrench from our <a href="/best-torque-wrench/">torque wrench guide</a> is the ambitious choice, and a small <a href="/best-shop-vac/">wet/dry shop vac</a> is the gift that cleans up after all of it.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">For the cook and the griller</h3>

          <p>
            Cookware is one of the most reliable gift categories for men who cook, because good pans last for decades and most men are still using whatever came with their first apartment. The Lodge 12-inch skillet is the best value on this page. The HexClad and the Le Creuset are the splurges, and all three come from our <a href="/best-induction-cookware/">induction cookware guide</a>, which matters if he has an induction stove: every one of them works on it.
          </p>

          <p>
            For the man who lives at the grill, a fast instant-read thermometer is the gift that changes results most. It stops the cut-and-peek habit that dries out steaks and makes chicken safe without guesswork. Pair the Thermapen with the Lodge and he has a complete steak night.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="outdoors-coffee-tech" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Cool Christmas Gifts for Men: Outdoors, Coffee, Grooming and Tech
          </h2>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">For the outdoorsman</h3>

          <p>
            Outdoor gifts work best when they make a trip easier rather than adding gear to carry. A compact power station like the EcoFlow River 3, the Best Compact pick in our <a href="/best-portable-power-station/">portable power station guide</a>, keeps phones, lights and a laptop running at camp. A pair of Hestra leather gloves, the Best Overall pick in our <a href="/best-ski-gloves/">ski gloves guide</a>, is the winter gift skiers and anyone who works outside appreciate every cold morning.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">For the coffee guy</h3>

          <p>
            Coffee gifts are easy to get right because the man in question has already told you what he cares about every morning. If he makes pour-over, the Fellow Stagg EKG, our top pick in our <a href="/best-electric-kettle/">electric kettle guide</a>, is the most giftable appliance on this list. The OXO gooseneck covers most of the same ground for less money, and the AeroPress is the under-$50 gift that turns a coffee drinker into a coffee tinkerer.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">For grooming</h3>

          <p>
            Grooming gifts are where people most often guess wrong, so choose tools that work for any style. The OneBlade 360 trims, edges and shaves, which suits almost every face. For the man who has mentioned his back, the BAKblade from our <a href="/best-mens-back-shavers/">men's back shaver guide</a> is a practical gift, and our guide on <a href="/how-to-shave-back-hair/">how to shave back hair</a> covers the technique.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">For the tech and home-gadget guy</h3>

          <p>
            Tech gifts are the most popular Christmas gifts for men and also the easiest to get wrong, because they depend on what he already owns. AirPods Pro 3 are excellent for an iPhone user and a poor choice for an Android user. The new 2026 Kindle Paperwhite is a safer bet, since it works on its own and suits anyone who reads, or used to. For the man who trains at home, adjustable dumbbells or a single kettlebell from our <a href="/best-home-gym-equipment-on-a-budget/">budget home gym guide</a> get used far more than most fitness gadgets.
          </p>
        </div>

